    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "There has been some progress on this issue but it isn't completely fixed. I think the main restriction is that for large FFTs the FFT length must be factorizable into primes smaller than 127, which is a limitation we inherit from https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cufft/index.html#function-cufftmakeplanmany64\r\n\r\nOther than that it's possible things just work now with a jaxlib built from head.",
